// @test: run-interpreter
// @level: L0
// @tier: 0
// @tags: stdlib-runtime, uuid, archive, wanted-set
// @expected-stdout: version 4

// `core/id/uuid.vr:109` calls `core.sys.common.random_bytes(buf)` by
// ABSOLUTE PATH rather than through a mount, and that module calls
// `super.darwin.libsystem.safe_getentropy` the same way. The dep graph
// records such a call as the MODULE that owns the callee — no trailing
// item name — so the archive-decode side, which matched an edge by its
// last segment against a wanted simple name, could never see it, and
// `v4()` died with "stage-3 uniquely-named public free fn stub to
// 'safe_getentropy' never resolved".
//
// Adding EITHER `core.sys.common.{random_bytes}` or
// `core.sys.darwin.libsystem.{safe_getentropy}` to the programme's own
// mount list made it answer 4, so the bodies were in the archive all
// along and only the decode set was short. Twenty-one tests in
// core-tests/base/uuid sat on this one stub.
//
// The mount list here is deliberately the SHORT one: naming anything
// further would repair the very input under test.
//
// CLOSED 2026-09-14 (T1481). The decode set now widens along CALL edges,
// and it names the FUNCTION rather than its module — a module in the
// wanted set is a wholesale mount, and that version answered this file
// correctly while taking `hello world` from 0.61 s of user time to 249 s.
// Measured on the fix: this programme answers in 5.9 s of user time and
// `hello world` is unchanged at 0.65 s.
//
// TWO MECHANISMS WERE NAMED AND BOTH REFUTED WITH INSTRUMENTS, which is
// why they are written down rather than re-tried:
//
//   * the DECODE set is not the gate. `core.sys.darwin` is already among
//     the decoded entries in the failing run — archive entries are coarse
//     and `libsystem` has none of its own. A change that widened the
//     prefix set from 36 to 3964 through the dep graph's module edges
//     moved the decoded entry count 24 -> 36 and did not fix this;
//     it was reverted.
//
//   * the mount PRUNE is not the gate either: `VERUM_NO_MOUNT_PRUNE=1`
//     reproduces the panic unchanged.
//
// What the tree's own tracer says is exact:
//
//     [remap-fallback] tier2 MISS archive_id=4278189098
//     archive_name="safe_getentropy" not in ctx_func_by_name
//     OR archive_func_by_name
//
// so the function was decoded and never REGISTERED — `register_module_filtered`
// keeps only the wanted subset, and the archive-wide name index is built from
// what registration kept. The name is wanted by a body that is MERGED, not by
// the user's mount list, and nothing feeds that back.

mount core.prelude.*;
mount core.id.uuid.{Uuid, v4};

fn main() {
    let u = v4();
    print(f"version {u.version()}");
}
